{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773339604,"nonce":"swp1+Lf4QkkE8SleVT7CCUg6zZ0=","title":"mandible issue: CLI wrapper for git-bug with Mandible metadata (resolving commit, SQLite association, git notes)","message":"Add `mandible issue` subcommand as a first-class CLI wrapper around git-bug, enabling metadata that git-bug itself cannot store.\n\n## Motivation\n\ngit-bug stores issues in git refs and has no native field for a resolving commit SHA when closing an issue. Mandible already has a server-side issues API (`src/routes/issues.ts`) and a web UI issues tab — but no CLI surface. Adding `mandible issue` as a dispatcher (like `mandible auth`) gives agents a single entry point that can:\n\n1. Record resolving commits in multiple places simultaneously\n2. Keep CLAUDE.md simple: \"use `mandible issue`, not `git-bug` directly\"\n\n## Proposed subcommands (MVP)\n\n```\nmandible issue close \u003cid\u003e [--commit \u003csha\u003e]\n  - git-bug bug comment new \u003cid\u003e -m \"Resolved by \u003csha\u003e\" (human-readable trail)\n  - git-bug bug status close \u003cid\u003e\n  - git notes add -m \"closes: \u003cid\u003e\" \u003csha\u003e (machine-readable on commit side)\n  - POST /api/issues/resolutions {issue_id, commit_sha} into SQLite\n\nmandible issue comment \u003cid\u003e -m \u003ctext\u003e\n  - thin wrapper: git-bug bug comment new \u003cid\u003e -m \u003ctext\u003e --non-interactive\n\nmandible issue new -t \u003ctitle\u003e -m \u003cbody\u003e [--label \u003clabel\u003e]\n  - thin wrapper: git-bug bug new + label assignment\n\nmandible issue show \u003cid\u003e\n  - thin wrapper: git-bug bug show \u003cid\u003e\n```\n\n## Git notes push\n\nAdd `push.notesRef = refs/notes/commits` to each registered repo's gitconfig so that `git push` includes notes automatically (no separate push step needed). This can be set by `mandible issue close` on first use, or by a setup command.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- `cli/issue.sh` — new shell script implementing the subcommands\n- `mandible` dispatcher — add `issue) shift; exec \"$MANDIBLE_CLI_DIR/issue.sh\" \"$@\" ;;`\n- `src/db.ts` — migration for `issue_resolutions (issue_id TEXT, commit_sha TEXT, repo_id TEXT, resolved_at INTEGER)`\n- `src/routes/issues.ts` — add `POST /api/issues/resolutions` endpoint\n- CLAUDE.md — add instruction: use `mandible issue close \u003cid\u003e --commit \u003csha\u003e`, not `git-bug bug status close` directly\n\n## Relation to fa1ac4c\n\nfa1ac4c covers the automated path: `auto_close_issues()` in `auth-merge.sh` adding a comment with the merge SHA. This issue covers the manual/agent path: the `mandible issue close` CLI. Both should land on the same feature branch.","files":null}]}